        },
        "pageimage": "The_Moon_Is_A_Harsh_Mistress_(book).jpg",
        "extract": "The Moon Is a Harsh Mistress is a 1966 science fiction novel by American writer Robert A. Heinlein about a 2075 revolt by a lunar penal colony against Earth's rule. Three million \"Loonies\" (lunar inhabitants) live in underground cities where a virtually anarcho-capitalist society has developed. When the Federated Nations threaten the colony's resources, computer technician Manuel \"Mannie\" O'Kelly-Davis, political agitator Wyoming Knott, and rational-anarchist Professor Bernardo de la Paz join forces with \"Mike,\" a self-aware supercomputer, to plan an independence movement timed to culminate on July 4, 2076. \nThe novel explores libertarian ideals...",
